## Description

This detection identifies the execution of **Windows Management Instrumentation (WMI)** queries performed through **PowerShell's Get-CimInstance cmdlet** using **Microsoft Sysmon Event ID 1 (Process Creation)**.

Windows Management Instrumentation (WMI) provides access to operating system, hardware, software, and management information. Modern PowerShell uses **Get-CimInstance** to query WMI objects via the Common Information Model (CIM).

Threat actors frequently abuse WMI for system reconnaissance, remote execution, lateral movement, and persistence.

Monitoring Get-CimInstance execution helps defenders detect reconnaissance activity and identify suspicious administrative behavior.

