# Analyst Notes

Windows Management Instrumentation (WMI) is one of the most valuable administrative frameworks available on Windows. It is also heavily abused by attackers for reconnaissance, remote execution, and post-exploitation.

PowerShell's Get-CimInstance cmdlet is the modern replacement for Get-WmiObject and is commonly observed during legitimate administration. Analysts should pay particular attention to repeated CIM queries, execution by unexpected users, or CIM activity occurring alongside PowerShell abuse, credential access, or lateral movement.

This detection provides valuable visibility into system reconnaissance and complements other PowerShell-based detections within this Splunk Detection Engineering project.
